    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d943">

                <pb facs="0901" n="587" sameAs="frus:frus1914Supp/pg587"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 763.72111G27/8</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State to the German
                        Ambassador</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Bernstorff</hi>)</head>
                <dateline>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State</hi>, <lb/>
                    <placeName>
                        <hi rendition="#italic">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                        calendar="gregorian" when="1914-11-07">
                        <hi rendition="#italic">November 7, 1914</hi>.</date>
                </dateline>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">My dear Mr. Ambassador</hi>: Referring to my
                    previous communication to you of October 30 regarding the internment of the
                    German cruiser <hi rendition="#italic">Geier</hi>, the Department is now in
                    possession of information that the German steamship <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Locksun</hi>, belonging to the Norddeutscher Lloyd Company, cleared August
                    16, 1914, from Manila with 3,215 tons of coal for Menado, in the Celebes; that
                    she coaled the German warship <hi rendition="#italic">Geier</hi> in the course
                    of her voyage toward Honolulu, where she arrived soon after the <hi
                        rendition="#italic">Geier</hi>; that the <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Locksun</hi> received coal by transfer from another vessel somewhere
                    between Manila and Honolulu; and that the captain stated that he had on board
                    245 or 250 tons of coal when he entered Honolulu, whereas investigation showed
                    that he had on board approximately 1,600 tons.</p>
                <p>From these facts the Department is of the opinion that the operations of the <hi
                        rendition="#italic">Locksun</hi> constitute her a tender to the <hi
                        rendition="#italic">Geier</hi>, and that she may be reasonably so considered
                    at the present time. This Government is, therefore, under the necessity of
                    according the <hi rendition="#italic">Locksun</hi> the same treatment as the <hi
                        rendition="#italic">Geier</hi>, and has taken steps to have the vessel
                    interned at Honolulu if she does not leave immediately.</p>
                <p>I am [etc.]</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Robert Lansing</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
